    {
      "id": "qEDvQ-qh-5V2kLoTC",
      "name": "69",
      "reference": "Sol:10",
      "reference_highlight": "69",
      "local_notes": "**Defaults:** Oral-2 or Erotic Art-3  \n**Prerequisite:** Oral  \n**Maximum:** Oral  \n**Stimulation:** **5(3)** to each participant\n\nThis is simultaneous mutual oral stimulation. Each participant rolls their own 69 technique; that roll determines the Stimulation they provide to the other partner. A success therefore gives the other participant 5 Stimulation, while an ordinary failure gives 3. Resolve critical success and critical failure normally for each roll.\n\nThe technique assumes both partners are actively participating. If only one partner is providing oral stimulation, use **Oral** instead.\n\nBecause receiving does not itself require a skill roll, a participant may be much better at giving than their partner without changing what they receive.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques.",
      "tags": [
        "Sexual"
      ],
      "difficulty": "a",
      "default": {
        "type": "skill",
        "name": {
          "compare": "is",
          "qualifier": "Oral"
        },
        "modifier": -2
      },
      "limit": 0,
      "prereqs": {
        "type": "prereq_list",
        "all": true,
        "prereqs": [
          {
            "type": "skill_prereq",
            "has": true,
            "name": {
              "compare": "is",
              "qualifier": "Oral"
            },
            "level": {
              "compare": "at_least"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "points": 1
    },
