    {
      "id": "q2fa_j107fUgiuge8",
      "name": "Auto-Knotting",
      "reference": "Sol:17",
      "reference_highlight": "Auto-Knotting",
      "local_notes": "**Default:** \\[lower of Auto-Fellatio (Oral) and Knot-Tying]-4  \n**Prerequisites:** Auto-Fellatio (Oral) 12+, Knot-Tying 12+, and Exotic Genitalia  \n**Maximum:** Lower of Auto-Fellatio (Oral) or Knot-Tying  \n**Stimulation:** **8(3)**\n\nThe character simultaneously performs Auto-Fellatio, acts as the receiving partner, and aligns their own locking anatomy. The lock remains primarily in the mouth and is not intended to deeply obstruct the airway.\n\n**Success:** The lock seats correctly; 8 Stimulation.  \n**Failure:** The lock fails to seat correctly, but the underlying self-oral contact still gives 3 Stimulation.  \n**Critical failure:** Lose **1 FP** from gagging/breath disruption, make an immediate Mating-Lock Management or Stuffing roll if the lock engaged badly, and apply the normal critical-failure loss of an Arousal Level.\n\nA character with **Doesn't Breathe** ignores the 1 FP breathing consequence but not bad alignment, injury, or the Arousal-Level effect.\n\nThe generic +3 self-use modifier does not stack with Auto-Knotting.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques.\n\nGCS selection required: replace @Lower of Auto-Fellatio (Oral) and Knot-Tying@ with the exact name of the applicable learned technique. For a lower-of rule, select the lower current level and recheck after either technique changes.",
