    {
      "id": "qgFfZYzNAC5aT3am6",
      "name": "Frost Kiss",
      "reference": "Sol:16",
      "reference_highlight": "Frost Kiss",
      "local_notes": "**Defaults:** Oral-4 or Erotic Art-6  \n**Prerequisites:** Oral 12+; Cold Breath with enough control to produce a harmless trace/trickle of cold  \n**Maximum:** Oral  \n**Stimulation:** **7(2)**\n\nFrost Kiss is a threshold-timing Oral technique. The performer reads the recipient's responses, stops Oral at the brink of climax, applies an extremely brief and deliberately noninjurious trace of supernatural cold to the genitals, and immediately resumes Oral so that the returning warmth creates the intended contrast.\n\nFrost Kiss may be attempted as a special technique only while the recipient is in **Plateau or Orgasmic**. If used earlier, resolve the action as ordinary Oral instead.\n\n**Success:** 7 Stimulation.  \n**Success by 5+ while the recipient is Orgasmic:** Add **+2 Stimulation**.  \n**Failure:** 2 Stimulation; the timing or transition is imperfect.  \n**Critical failure:** Apply the normal loss of one Arousal Level.\n\nThe Cold Breath prerequisite assumes the user can reduce the effect to a harmless output. If the underlying power requires a specific enhancement, perk, or control roll to do that, that requirement still applies.\n\nFor critical success, double the base Frost Kiss Stimulation first, then add the +2 threshold bonus if applicable; the +2 bonus itself is not doubled.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques.",
