    {
      "id": "qEZNocNhUD2ZC8KXw",
      "name": "Mating-Lock Management",
      "reference": "Sol:14",
      "reference_highlight": "Mating-Lock Management",
      "local_notes": "**Defaults:** Stuffing-2 or Erotic Art-4  \n**Prerequisites:** Stuffing 12+ or Erotic Art 12+; the partner's anatomy must actually be capable of locking  \n**Maximum:** Stuffing or Erotic Art, whichever default is being used  \n**Stimulation:** None\n\nThis is the **receiving-side** technique for deliberately accepting, maintaining, and later safely releasing a mating lock: knot, bulb, locking ridge, barbs, or similar anatomy.\n\nRoll when the lock first attempts to seat, or again when a difficult change of posture, movement, or release makes management relevant.\n\n**Success:** The lock seats comfortably and may be maintained safely.  \n**Failure:** The lock cannot be safely exploited; either it fails to seat cleanly or the participants must reduce intensity/position until the problem is corrected.  \n**Critical failure:** Treat the result as an appropriate Stuffing-type injury risk.\n\nThis technique does not itself provide Stimulation. The underlying penetration technique continues to determine Stimulation.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques.",
