    {
      "id": "qQeTo5nxV_T4KVpYa",
      "name": "Prehensile Appendage Play",
      "reference": "Sol:15",
      "reference_highlight": "Prehensile Appendage Play",
      "local_notes": "**Defaults:** Masturbation (appropriate physiology)-2 or Erotic Art-2  \n**Prerequisite:** A functional prehensile appendage capable of fine manipulation  \n**Maximum:** Erotic Art+4  \n**Stimulation:** **4(2)** to the recipient\n\nThis technique covers deliberate sexual manipulation with a prehensile tail, tongue, genital appendage, tentacle, trunk, or similar anatomy. Merely being flexible is not sufficient; the appendage must be able to position itself with meaningful control.\n\nThe listed Stimulation is to the **recipient**. The user does not automatically gain Stimulation unless the appendage itself is erogenous and another rule or technique provides it.\n\nPhysiological modifiers may apply when the user is unfamiliar with the recipient's species or anatomy. A character familiar with a ubiquitous Sol Mahina physiology may ignore such penalties at the GM's discretion.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques.",
