      "local_notes": "**Source:** September 21 discussion; working technique with explicit user clarifications.  \n**Defaults:** Erotic Art-1, HT-3, or Holdout-3  \n**Prerequisite:** Erotic Art and suitable receptive anatomy  \n**Maximum:** Erotic Art  \n**Stimulation:** None\n\nThis is the receiving-side accommodation check for the relevant nonhuman anatomy. Roll when accommodation is required; the active technique supplies any Stimulation separately.\n\n| Result | Recovered rule |\n|---|---|\n| Success | Comfortable accommodation. |\n| Ordinary failure | Accommodation is conditional or needs adjustment; the recovered proposal did not specify a separate universal injury amount. |\n| Critical failure | Possible injury/FP consequences appropriate to the existing accommodation subsystem; an exact independent damage formula was not recovered. |\n\n| Modifier | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| High Pain Threshold | +2 |\n| Will 12+ | +1 total |\n| Each applicable **incoming** Large Penis level | −2 |\n| Tight Slit / unfamiliar physiology | A further −2 was proposed where applicable; not a universal automatic penalty. |\n\n**September 21 correction:** A character's own resident anatomy does not count as incoming size. Tsar's Will 50 still grants only the listed +1 Will-threshold bonus. With High Pain Threshold, his baseline bonus is **+3** before applicable incoming-size and other situational penalties.\n\nIndependent sources use their own relevant accommodation checks. Several active partners stimulating one recipient do not automatically turn the recipient into the performer of Double Play.\n\nGCS use: choose one default variant for a purchased technique. A maximum tied to another skill, or the lower of two skills, must be checked against the named skill(s); the native limit field is relative to the selected default. Apply situational modifiers to the roll, not as bonuses to all Erotic Art techniques."
